 hostages in order to make it out alive.\",\"__typename\":\"MovieLocalized\",\"sdTeasers\":[],\"hdTeasers\":[],\"poster\":{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/4d/8e/4d8e8693e2fd996c6e2520ddcc06f336.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},\"sdTrailers\":[],\"hdTrailers\":[],\"cmsAssets\":{\"__typename\":\"CMSAsset\",\"images\":[]}},\"cast\":{\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\",\"nodes\":[{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"George\",\"lastName\":\"Clooney\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Quentin\",\"lastName\":\"Tarantino\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Harvey\",\"lastName\":\"Keitel\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Juliette\",\"lastName\":\"Lewis\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Ernest\",\"lastName\":\"Liu\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Salma\",\"lastName\":\"Hayek\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Cheech\",\"lastName\":\"Marin\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Danny\",\"lastName\":\"Trejo\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Tom\",\"lastName\":\"Savini\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Fred\",\"lastName\":\"Williamson\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null}]},\"releases\":[{\"releasedAt\":\"1996-05-09T00:00:00.000Z\",\"__typename\":\"Release\",\"localRatings\":[],\"rating\":{\"advisory\":null,\"__typename\":\"Rating\",\"certificate\":\"18\"},\"distributors\":[{\"id\":\"16219\",\"name\":\"Walt Disney\",\"__typename\":\"Company\"}]}],\"embargoes\":[],\"exhibitor\":{\"title\":null,\"poster\":null,\"synopsis\":null,\"__typename\":\"MovieLocalizedOverride\",\"images\":[]},\"originalTitle\":\"From Dusk till Dawn\",\"synopsis\":\"The Gecko brothers, two dangerous outlaws on a wild crime spree, kidnap a father and his two kids and head south to a seedy Mexican bar to hide out in safety. Soon they realize that they're not in a typical bar, as the entire place begins to teem with vicious, blood-sucking vampires. With the odds stacked greatly against them, the Geckos are forced to team up with their hostages in order to make it out alive.\",\"certificate\":\"18\",\"casting\":[\"George Clooney\",\"Quentin Tarantino\",\"Harvey Keitel\",\"Juliette Lewis\",\"Ernest Liu\",\"Salma Hayek\",\"Cheech Marin\",\"Danny Trejo\",\"Tom Savini\",\"Fred Williamson\"],\"direction\":[\"Robert Rodriguez\"],\"coDirection\":[],\"pictures\":[\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/pictures/15/10/28/17/27/104559.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/62/83/60/19076756.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/62/83/60/19076753.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/62/83/60/19076754.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/02/22/19883398.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/02/22/19883397.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/02/22/19883396.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/62/83/60/19076752.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/62/83/60/19076751.jpg\"],\"heroImages\":[],\"release\":\"1996-05-09T00:00:00.000Z\",\"advisory\":null,\"trailer\":{\"SD\":null,\"HD\":null},\"localizations\":[],\"studio\":{\"name\":\"Walt Disney\"}},{\"id\":\"1000046327\",\"title\":\"GIANT - The Play\",\"runtime\":8160,\"genres\":\"Drama\",\"__typename\":\"Movie\",\"altId\":[\"418643\"],\"poster\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/1e/90/1e90e7cd129cc657105dbdd7ce482daf.jpg\",\"coDirectors\":{\"nodes\":[],\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\"},\"images\":[{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/36/82/3682b7724764d7d7e7e9e03ebf193485.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/89/8e/898ec26fb60f3b338264ddc1cd3452d2.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/c6/57/c657d4fb52251f1626094f4ce725af4f.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/9a/59/9a5913f652a757a50dab302665b35f40.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/d9/dc/d9dcc807f8ea776c797d0d8532cd2265.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/da/6b/da6b9710059def6f0fd855faffb87be8.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/ce/c6/cec6c1fbb3a67621e6eff732e854d384.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"}],\"quadImages\":[\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/74/ce/74ce316575cc0cdac1cc19f3c95ff462.jpg\"],\"directors\":{\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\",\"nodes\":[{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"person\":{\"firstName\":\"Nicholas\",\"lastName\":\"Hytner\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"}}]},\"locale\":{\"title\":\"GIANT - The Play\",\"synopsis\":\"GIANT, the 5-star critically acclaimed play starring John Lithgow (Killers of the Flower Moon, The Crown) as Roald Dahl, comes to the big screen. Winner of 3 Olivier Awards® including Best Play and a Tony Award® for Best Actor in a Play (John Lithgow), the production was filmed live in London’s West End ahead of its sold-out Broadway run. The stellar cast includes Aya Cash (The Boys, The Franchise, You’re the Worst), Elliot Levey (Cold War, Patriots, Good) and Rachael Stirling (The Divine Mrs S). A world-famous children’s author under threat. A battle of wills in the wake of scandal. And one chance to make amends...It’s the summer of 1983, The Witches is about to hit the shelves and Roald Dahl is making last-minute edits. But the outcry at his recent, explicitly antisemitic article won’t die down. Across a single afternoon at his family home, and rocked by an unexpectedly explosive confrontation, Dahl is forced to choose: make a public apology or risk his name and reputation. Inspired by real events, GIANT explores with dark humour the difference between considered opinion and dangerous rhetoric offering a complicated portrait of a fiendishly charismatic icon.\",\"__typename\":\"MovieLocalized\",\"sdTeasers\":[],\"hdTeasers\":[],\"poster\":{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/1e/90/1e90e7cd129cc657105dbdd7ce482daf.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},\"sdTrailers\":[{\"url\":\"https://m.boxoffice.media/mp4/418643_uk_high.mp4\",\"__typename\":\"MovieVideo\"}],\"hdTrailers\":[{\"url\":\"https://m.boxoffice.media/QuickTime/418643_uk_hd.mov\",\"__typename\":\"MovieVideo\"}],\"cmsAssets\":{\"__typename\":\"CMSAsset\",\"images\":[]}},\"cast\":{\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\",\"nodes\":[{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"John\",\"lastName\":\"Lithgow\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Elliot\",\"lastName\":\"Levey\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Aya\",\"lastName\":\"Cash\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Rachael\",\"lastName\":\"Stirling\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Tessa\",\"lastName\":\"Bonham Jones\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Richard\",\"lastName\":\"Hope\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null}]},\"releases\":[{\"releasedAt\":\"2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z\",\"__typename\":\"Release\",\"localRatings\":[],\"distributors\":[{\"id\":\"39223\",\"name\":\"Trafalgar Releasing\",\"__typename\":\"Company\"}],\"rating\":{\"advisory\":null,\"__typename\":\"Rating\",\"certificate\":\"15\"}}],\"embargoes\":[],\"exhibitor\":{\"title\":null,\"poster\":null,\"synopsis\":null,\"__typename\":\"MovieLocalizedOverride\",\"images\":[]},\"originalTitle\":\"GIANT - The Play\",\"synopsis\":\"GIANT, the 5-star critically acclaimed play starring John Lithgow (Killers of the Flower Moon, The Crown) as Roald Dahl, comes to the big screen. Winner of 3 Olivier Awards® including Best Play and a Tony Award® for Best Actor in a Play (John Lithgow), the production was filmed live in London’s West End ahead of its sold-out Broadway run. The stellar cast includes Aya Cash (The Boys, The Franchise, You’re the Worst), Elliot Levey (Cold War, Patriots, Good) and Rachael Stirling (The Divine Mrs S). A world-famous children’s author under threat. A battle of wills in the wake of scandal. And one chance to make amends...It’s the summer of 1983, The Witches is about to hit the shelves and Roald Dahl is making last-minute edits. But the outcry at his recent, explicitly antisemitic article won’t die down. Across a single afternoon at his family home, and rocked by an unexpectedly explosive confrontation, Dahl is forced to choose: make a public apology or risk his name and reputation. Inspired by real events, GIANT explores with dark humour the difference between considered opinion and dangerous rhetoric offering a complicated portrait of a fiendishly charismatic icon.\",\"certificate\":\"15\",\"casting\":[\"John Lithgow\",\"Elliot Levey\",\"Aya Cash\",\"Rachael Stirling\",\"Tessa Bonham Jones\",\"Richard Hope\"],\"direction\":[\"Nicholas Hytner\"],\"coDirection\":[],\"pictures\":[\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/36/82/3682b7724764d7d7e7e9e03ebf193485.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/89/8e/898ec26fb60f3b338264ddc1cd3452d2.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/c6/57/c657d4fb52251f1626094f4ce725af4f.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/9a/59/9a5913f652a757a50dab302665b35f40.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/d9/dc/d9dcc807f8ea776c797d0d8532cd2265.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/da/6b/da6b9710059def6f0fd855faffb87be8.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/ce/c6/cec6c1fbb3a67621e6eff732e854d384.jpg\"],\"heroImages\":[],\"release\":\"2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z\",\"advisory\":null,\"trailer\":{\"SD\":\"https://m.boxoffice.media/mp4/418643_uk_high.mp4\",\"HD\":\"https://m.boxoffice.media/QuickTime/418643_uk_hd.mov\"},\"localizations\":[],\"studio\":{\"name\":\"Trafalgar Releasing\"},\"orderIndex\":59},{\"id\":\"298853\",\"title\":\"Glenrothan\",\"runtime\":5820,\"genres\":\"Drama\",\"poster\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/e7/2e/e72e5ea78231ca0a780f252aef51e3d7.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Movie\",\"altId\":[\"378042\"],\"coDirectors\":{\"nodes\":[],\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\"},\"images\":[],\"quadImages\":[],\"locale\":{\"title\":\"Glenrothan\",\"synopsis\":\"Two brothers following a violent exchange with their father on the day of their mother's funeral, the younger of the two left their Highland home for America. After forty years they reunite in the land of their birth.\",\"__typename\":\"MovieLocalized\",\"sdTeasers\":[],\"hdTeasers\":[],\"poster\":{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/e7/2e/e72e5ea78231ca0a780f252aef51e3d7.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},\"sdTrailers\":[{\"url\":\"https://m.boxoffice.media/mp4/378042_uk_high.mp4\",\"__t